  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Encoding and ASCII"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Encoding is the mechanism of converting data into an equivalent code using a fixed scheme, so that every computer reads it the same way. ASCII (American Standard Code for Information Interchange) is a 7-bit code, so it can represent $2^7 = 128$ characters: English letters, digits, punctuation and control characters. In ASCII, A–Z are 65–90, a–z are 97–122, the digits 0–9 are 48–57 and the space is 32."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "ASCII: 7 bits → 128 characters"
    },
    {
     "en": "'A' = 65, 'a' = 97, '0' = 48, space = 32"
    },
    {
     "en": "Lower-case code = upper-case code + 32"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Encoding is the mechanism of converting data into an equivalent code using a fixed scheme, so that every computer reads it the same way. ASCII (American Standard Code for Information Interchange) is a 7-bit code, so it can represent $2^7 = 128$ characters: English letters, digits, punctuation and control characters. In ASCII, A–Z are 65–90, a–z are 97–122, the digits 0–9 are 48–57 and the space is 32.",
    "kn": "ಸಂಕೇತೀಕರಣ ಎಂದರೆ ನಿಗದಿತ ಪದ್ಧತಿಯಿಂದ ದತ್ತಾಂಶವನ್ನು ಸಮಾನ ಸಂಕೇತಕ್ಕೆ ಬದಲಿಸುವುದು. ASCII 7-ಬಿಟ್ ಸಂಕೇತ; ಅದು 128 ಅಕ್ಷರಗಳನ್ನು ಪ್ರತಿನಿಧಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. A–Z = 65–90, a–z = 97–122, 0–9 = 48–57."
   },
   "formula": "\\text{characters} = 2^{\\text{bits}}"
  },
